  "details": "Notify users if the world they're currently in has broken networking.\nThe prompt should ask users to create a new instance or to update VRChat.\n**Details**\nWhen VRChat or a world is updated, clients can calculate different network IDs for the same object. This will break most networking related interactions or Udon code in a world.\nWorld creators can detect broken networking easily. In my world, I wait variables to be received by a client from the master. If this never happens, an animation plays that informs the user that something is wrong.\nIt would be convenient if this functionality was built into VRChat itself, as networking issues can affect most worlds. However, most world creators have no scripts in place to warn users about the broken state of a world.",
